language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Diamond-free degree sequences: find a simple undirected graph on N vertices, given by its adjacency matrix, whose degrees are non-increasing, positive and divisible by 3, with degree sum divisible by 12, and that contains no diamond (no four vertices with at least five edges between them).
given N : int
find matrix_ : matrix indexed by [int(1..N), int(1..N)] of bool
find deg : matrix indexed by [int(1..N)] of int(0..N-1)

branching on [matrix_]
such that
$ the graph is simple and undirected: no loop edges, and the edge between u and v is the same edge as between v and u
forAll i : int(1..N) . !matrix_[i, i],
forAll i, j : int(1..N) . matrix_[i, j] = matrix_[j, i],
$ the degree of each vertex is the number of its adjacent vertices
forAll i : int(1..N) . deg[i] = (sum j : int(1..N) . matrix_[i, j]),
$ the degrees are listed in non-increasing order, d_i >= d_(i+1)
forAll i : int(1..N-1) . deg[i] >= deg[i + 1],
$ each degree is greater than zero and divisible by 3 (modulo 3 is zero)
forAll i : int(1..N) . deg[i] > 0 /\ deg[i] % 3 = 0,
$ the sum of the degrees is divisible by 12 (so the number of edges is divisible by 6)
((sum i : int(1..N) . deg[i]) % 12) = 0,
$ diamond-free: for every set of four vertices the number of edges between them is at most four
forAll a : int(1..N) . forAll b : int(a+1..N) . forAll c : int(b+1..N) . forAll d : int(c+1..N) . (matrix_[a, b] + matrix_[a, c] + matrix_[a, d] + matrix_[b, c] + matrix_[b, d] + matrix_[c, d]) <= 4
